# The mistake bubble's two board-click lines, on a board where nothing else moves. Seat 0 (alice)
# has priority in an uncontested turn-1 Main Phase 1 with a Runeclaw Bear that came in this turn:
# pressing it is refused ("not-offered", summoning sick) and says the "sick" line. Seat 1 (bob)
# holds a Forest he cannot play on alice's turn: pressing it is refused ("no-input", no priority)
# and says the "priority" line. Nothing Forge sends follows either press, so the bubble shows only
# because the press itself redraws the board. Used by `e2e/mistake-bubbles.spec.ts`.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Runeclaw Bear|SummonSick
humanlibrary=Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest
humangraveyard=
aihand=Forest
aibattlefield=
ailibrary=Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest
aigraveyard=
